      ],
      "source": "https://www.bpks.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after Olive North's hometown, Belle Plaine, Iowa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bpks.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In its first decade, Belle Plaine boasted a stagecoach stop, carriage factory, and a bustling grain elevator.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bpks.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Three railroads serviced Belle Plaine: AT&S on the west edge, Missouri-Pacific on the south edge, and Midland Valley on the east.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bpks.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Belle Plaine hosts an annual Downtown Festival that celebrates local culture and community spirit.",
